# What NOT to ship in the VSIX.
#
# `vsce` ignores `.gitignore` entirely. Without this file it packages the whole
# tree — including `PRD_Git_Control.md`, `src/`, `test/`, and the source maps with
# their embedded `sourcesContent` — plus the production `node_modules`, even
# though everything is already bundled into `dist/`.
#
# Everything the extension needs at runtime is `dist/`, `resources/`, and
# `package.json` (always included by vsce).

# Internal, never published.
PRD_Git_Control.md
**/*.md
.env
.env.*

# Sources: bundled into dist/, so shipping them doubles the package.
src/**
test/**
out/**
tsconfig.json
esbuild.js

# Source maps carry full `sourcesContent` and developer paths.
**/*.map

# Bundled by esbuild, so nothing is resolved from node_modules at runtime.
node_modules/**

# Tooling and local state.
.git/**
.gitignore
.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
**/*.vsix
